rb.question:
A sheet of 8-inch by 10-inch paper is placed on top of a sheet of $8 \frac{1}{2}$-inch by 11-inch paper, as shown. What is the area of the region of overlap in square inches?

[asy]draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,8)--(0,8)--(0,0)--cycle,linewidth(2));
draw((0,8)--(8.5,8)--(8.5,11.5)--(0,11.5)--(0,8)--cycle,linewidth(2));

draw((8.5,0)--(8.5,8),dashed);
[/asy]

Below is a magic square, meaning that the sum of the numbers in each row, in each column, and in each of the $2$ main diagonals are equal. What is the value of $n$?

[asy]size(125);
for(int i = 0; i<4; ++i)
{

draw((0,i)--(3,i),linewidth(1));
}

for(int j = 0; j<4; ++j)
{

draw((j,0)--(j,3),linewidth(1));
}

label("$n-3$",(.5,.5));
label("3",(.5,1.5));
label("$n+1$",(.5,2.5));

label("$n+2$",(1.5,.5));
label("$2n-9$",(1.5,1.5));
label("$1$",(1.5,2.5));

label("$2$",(2.5,.5));
label("$n$",(2.5,1.5));
label("$n-1$",(2.5,2.5));
[/asy]

rb.b:
By AM-GM,
\begin{align*}
x^4 + 4y^2 + 4z^4 &= x^4 + 2 \cdot 2y^2 + 2 \cdot 2z^4 \\
&\ge 4 \sqrt[4]{x^4 \cdot 2y^2 \cdot 2y^2 \cdot 2z^4 \cdot 2z^4} \\
&= 4 \sqrt[4]{16x^4 y^4 z^8} \\
&= 4 \sqrt[4]{16} \sqrt[4]{x^4 y^4 z^8} \\
&= 8 \sqrt[4]{x^4 y^4 z^8} \\
&= 8xy^2 z^2.
\end{align*}Since $xyz = 2,$ $y^2 z^2 = \frac{2}{x}.$  Hence,
\[8xy^2 z^2 = 8x \cdot \frac{2}{x} = 16.\]Equality occurs when $x^4 = 2y^2 = 2z^4,$ so $x^4 = \frac{1}{2} (4y^2) = \frac{1}{2} (4z^4).$  Then $x^4 = \frac{1}{2} (4y^2) = \frac{1}{2} (4z^4) = \frac{1}{2} \cdot $\begin{align*}
\boxed{16}
\end{align*}
